claim.claim-text:
identifying, by the first SMF, triggering of an SMF change operation;
performing a subscription procedure with an access and mobility management function, AMF, for an event in which a status of the UE becomes an idle or an inactive;
in case that the status of the LTE becomes the idle or the inactive, receiving, from the AMF, a notification message to report the event;
transmitting, to the AMF, a message indicating a change in a status of a protocol data unit, PDU, session so as to request a procedure of an SMF change, wherein the message indicating the change in the status of the PDU session includes a context identification, ID;
receiving a context request message requesting a context from a second SMF that is a target SMF; and
transmitting a context request response message to the second SMF.

performing a subscription procedure with a first session management function, SMF, for an event in which a status of the UE becomes an idle or an inactive;
in case that the status of the LTE becomes the idle or the inactive, transmitting, to the first SMF, a notification message to report the event;
receiving, from the first SMF, a message indicating a change in a status of a protocol data unit, PDU, session so as to request a procedure of an SMF change, wherein the message indicating the change in the status of the PDU session includes a context identification, ID;
identifying a second SMF that is a target SMF;
transmitting, to the second SMF, a request message of requesting generation of a new session; and
receiving, from the second SMF, a response message with respect to the request message of requesting generation of the new session.
